          },
          "summary": "Would you put your cell phone in all the hotels rooms you managed? I did and 10,000,000 guests later it was the most worthwhile thing I've done in my career. I also co-founded a company acquired by Amazon, sold a company to Marriott Vacations and spent half my career developing new technologies. I'm currently Chief Executive Officer of Hotel Equities, a leading hospitality management firm with a portfolio spanning North America, the Caribbean, and Latin America, which merged with Springboard Hospitality in spring 2025. I'm also managing director of Jororo, LLC, a private investment company focused on acquiring unique, independent hotels in Hawaii and across the mainland. Jororo currently has investments in eleven hotels representing ~1,800 rooms.Specialties: Emerging technology, e-commerce, analytics, hospitality."
